# Build output. The tree builds out of source, into build/, and nothing else
# is supposed to appear anywhere. The glob is for the second and third tree you
# end up with the moment anything is built two ways, which BUILD= is for:
# build-portable/ next to build/ is how the context switch gets checked both
# ways, and CI does the same thing under the same names.
build*/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
*.lib

# The generated amalgamation. It is a release artefact, produced by
# tools/burrow-gen, and checking it in would give us two sources of truth that
# differ on a Tuesday.
/burrow.c
/burrow.h
/burrow-crypto.c
/burrow-documented.h
dist/

# Fuzzing. Corpora live in burrow-conformance, crashes are triaged and then
# either fixed or committed there as a regression case.
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/crashes/
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Editors and platforms.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
compile_commands.json
.cache/
